------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party software and data
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Tributary includes software from third parties, each under its own license.
THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md lists every Go module compiled into the binary with
its full license text; the web interface's bundled packages and their
licenses ship with it as 3rdpartylicenses.txt.

Data sources:

* IP Geolocation by DB-IP (https://db-ip.com), licensed under the Creative
  Commons Attribution 4.0 International License (CC BY 4.0). Downloaded at
  runtime when "DB-IP Lite" is the selected GeoIP source (the default); the
  attribution is shown in the web interface.

* MaxMind GeoLite2 / GeoIP2 databases are only used when an administrator
  configures their own MaxMind account, under MaxMind's terms. When GeoLite2
  data is in use, the interface shows: "This product includes GeoLite2 data
  created by MaxMind, available from https://www.maxmind.com".

* MAC address vendor names: the built-in table is the Wireshark
  manufacturer database (https://www.wireshark.org), distributed by the
  Wireshark project (GPL-2.0-or-later) and compiled from the public IEEE
  Registration Authority registries, which Tributary can also download
  directly.

* ASNs missing from the local database may be looked up through the RIPEstat
  Data API (https://stat.ripe.net) when enabled, under RIPE NCC's terms.

Tributary stores flow data in ClickHouse (Apache License 2.0), which is
installed as a separate package and not distributed with Tributary.
